This repository holds @synorb/cli, the command-line client for the Synorb
REST API.

This is a synced, one-way mirror of cli/ in the private Synorb/synorb-v3
monorepo. A GitHub Action writes one generated commit to this repo's main
branch whenever the upstream path changes. Real development happens
upstream, not here.

Rules:
- Small documentation fixes (README wording, comments) are fine as direct
  PRs against this repo.
- Do not merge changes to src/cli.js, test/cli.test.js, or package.json
  scripts/dependencies directly into this repo. Open the PR for visibility,
  but note in the description that it needs to land upstream instead — the
  next sync overwrites anything committed here outside that pipeline.
- No build step, no framework, no bundler. Plain ES modules. Node 18.17+.
- Run tests with: npm test (runs node --test). No network access required.
- src/cli.js has no runtime dependencies beyond Node core modules and the
  global fetch.
- Match existing style: 2-space indent, double quotes, semicolons.
- Never put a credential in a URL or query string. Send it only via the
  Authorization: Bearer header. Never write a token anywhere but
  ~/.config/synorb/config.json (mode 0600).
- When adding a subcommand, update: the expectsValue set in parseArgs (if
  it takes a flag value), the command branch in run(), the HELP string,
  README.md, and test/cli.test.js.
